===Etymology 2===
A spelling representing the pronunciation ({{IPAchar|/miː/}}), which is the older pronunciation (see {{m+|enm|mi||my}}; {{m+|enm|me||me}} was pronounced /meː/, similar to modern ''[[May]]''); the {{w|Great Vowel Shift}} in the Middle Ages changed /iː/ to /aɪ/, but some dialects retained or reinnovated /iː/ in this word.

